  "description": "OKIFEV crystallizes in the hexagonal crystal system with space group P 63. Reported CIF formula moiety: C216 H232 Dy12 Na6 O88 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),5(C2 H3 N1),C1 H4 O1. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 4 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.812-3.839 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 107.94-109.78°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy12Na6(μ3-OH)4(OAc)12(L)12](NO3)2·(CH3CN)5·(CH3OH). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 12 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 12 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
